Voom's vfkit build is based on crc-org/vfkit v0.6.4
(f02465693e0cec8bb3b92a9d8324644c63a2e7f2), licensed under Apache-2.0.

Voom modifies vfkit to expose window titles, application names,
persistent GUI lifecycle options, display control over the existing REST
socket, and a capability probe. It also enforces read-only directory shares
in Virtualization.framework.
The vendored Code-Hex/vz v3.7.1 GUI bridge is modified to hide and reopen its
existing window, hide its Dock entry while the window is closed, set GUI menu
labels, read Voom's Help URL and About metadata from the app bundle, retain
the application event loop, and request graceful guest shutdown on Quit.
Its MIT license is included in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.

Upstream: https://github.com/crc-org/vfkit
GUI bindings: https://github.com/Code-Hex/vz
Patches: nix/patches/vfkit-gui.patch, nix/patches/vfkit-shares.patch, and
nix/patches/vz-gui.patch in Voom.
